|~ `::law`, the kind of a law, and the laws declared under it.
   The decisions it exists for: [D114]. ~|

:law
  |~~ A law is a claim about a name that runs: a query that answers
      true, a quote under this tag laid under the name whose behaviour it
      proves, its page the sentence of the claim. The chain of a function
      or a kind writes it by `proves`,
      `| proves :addsTheNumber |~~ Ten and three is thirteen. ~~| ~(10 | add 3 | eq 13)`,
      and a law of any other name is declared under it,
      `:limit/holdsTen ::law~(limit | eq 10)`.

      `laws` answers the laws of a name, each its page and its query,
      and `runLaws` runs them, so the examples of the catalog are its
      tests.
      ::link~(::any/laws | doc) ::link~(::any/runLaws | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/hypertext | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :provesItsClaim
        |~~ A law declared under a name proves its claim when it runs. ~~|
        ~(:k 5 | :k/answersFive |~~ k answers five. ~~| ::law~(k | eq 5) | ::k | runLaws | map /ok | eq [true])

